'''Historical package.''' SF Production Time is not in the current repository package list. Its package ID was <code>sf-production-time</code>.

The mod set timed production recipes to a chosen base duration. World speed settings continued to multiply that duration. Instant recipes and inventory quantities were preserved. The package targeted the client and Dedicated Server, requested the <code>patch</code> capability, and declared no runtime capability.

{| class="wikitable"
! Setting !! Key !! Default !! Range !! Effect
|-
| Base production time (seconds) || <code>seconds</code> || 1 second || 0.1–3600 seconds || Sets the base duration for timed recipes. The source guide instructed users to set the same value on the client and host or server before starting the game.
|}

The current [[Mod: Crafting Essentials|SF Crafting Essentials]] package provides two modes. Original recipe times can be scaled live while preserving relative durations. Shared-time mode sets one base duration for timed recipes during startup asset preparation. See that article for its settings, restart requirements, and production-speed behavior.

